{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the best of the land, etc. — let them dwell in the land of Goshen.</b> Now, one might have thought it would have been sufficient to say only ״בְּמֵיטַב הָאָרֶץ״, but since Yosef hinted in his words that he desired the land of Goshen, one might think that he did not want them to dwell in the land of Goshen, because he did not agree with his words. And if he had said only ״יֵשְׁבוּ בְּאֶרֶץ גֹּשֶׁן״, it would have been understood that he was providing them only with the land of Goshen and nothing better than it, if it seemed fit in Yosef's eyes — and this would contradict what he said earlier (Genesis 45:18): ״וְאֶתְּנָה לָכֶם אֶת טוּב אֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״. Therefore he said ״בְּמֵיטַב״ etc. ״בְּאֶרֶץ גֹּשֶׁן״. And this is the parsing of the verse: In the best of the land — settle them, etc., and I inform you that the land of Goshen is the best. And we find that Scripture itself testified thus, as it is written (Genesis 47:11): ״וַיּוֹשֵׁב יוֹסֵף״ etc. ״בְּמֵיטַב הָאָרֶץ בְּאֶרֶץ רַעְמְסֵס״ etc." "<b>Or</b> the parsing of the verse may be on this basis: <b>בְּמֵיטַב</b> etc., and if they chose for themselves the land of Goshen — let them dwell in it. And with this he did not definitively say that this is their place, but it remains at the threshold of willingness: if another place seems good in their eyes — the prerogative is in their hand to dwell in the best of the land."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:30.232256913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}